<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peng Dehuai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1898">1898</a>–<a href="/years/1974">1974</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peng Dehuai was a Chinese Communist general who commanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-volunteer-army">Chinese People's Volunteers</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korean-war">Korean War</a> from 1950 and later served as minister of defence. After he criticised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-leap-forward">Great Leap Forward</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-lu">Lushan</a> Conference of 1959 he was dismissed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>; persecuted during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cultural-revolution">Cultural Revolution</a>, he died in prison in 1974 and was rehabilitated in 1978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peng-dehuai.jpg" alt="Peng Dehuai" width="320" height="413" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ​《新华社》记者 郑景康 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Peng_Dehuai_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
